Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:19:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Budget v2: charge ACTUAL allocation (files + markers +
 entries) against maxBytes

2681e8a charged declared bytes only and let every file over-allocate by 64 MiB on its own:
a 1-byte zero-slack reservation allocated 8192 B and verify accepted it (root probe).

- blockBytes = real fs block (ext4/tmpfs only, checked before any write); sizes block-aligned
- slackBytes >= required_headroom (marker + entry + 2x extent tree per file, one step worst case)
- per-host BOOKKEEPING_BYTES for ledger/lock; ledger <= 64 KiB; markers <= 512 B
- allocate: projected bound before any write, bounded steps re-checked, actual bound at end
- verify: every local reservation's actual <= maxBytes; no per-file allowance
- holder: reservation blockBytes 4096, metadata alignment, slack >= required headroom
- tests: Accounting class incl. 2681e8a control; 11 new budget mutants
